fferent eigenvalue, will be linearly independent.\n\nNow, recall that ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ correspond to the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=1$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-5.$ Thus, the third eigenvector ${v}_{3}$ must correspond to ${\\lambda }_{3}=6.$ \n\nTo compute the eigenvectors of a matrix, we need to find non-zero solutions of the matrix equation \n\n$$\n(A-\\lambda I)\\text{x}=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =6.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 6\\end{bmatrix}-6\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -11 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the eigenvectors corresponding to this eigenvalue, we have to solve the corresponding homogeneous system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-5{x}_{1} &=0 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}-11{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSo, we row-reduce the augmented matrix $M$ to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -11 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} &  & {R}_{1}↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -11 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+5{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 10 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} &  & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are two pivot columns (the $1$st and the $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we obtain ${x}_{2}=0.$ From the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}=0.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting, for instance, ${x}_{3}=1,$ we get the following eigenvector:\n\n$$\nv=\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFinally, $\\frac{a}{c}=\\frac{0}{1}=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186392039 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392040 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392039 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392041 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392039 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392042 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392039 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392043 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392039 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392044 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392039 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392039 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392039 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186392042 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392039 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "60b86f5a-a5c7-5a8b-9d41-513f5f26be40" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392040 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392040 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392040 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "13304c66-59ed-5804-b519-223c3709ae32" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392041 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392041 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392041 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "317f7bc8-17c3-5b65-8500-5bfb85e37bde" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392042 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392042 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392042 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "808dfd35-c7cf-5560-bba9-dfef1206fd03" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392043 #edb/ref 1080 "-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392043 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392043 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "94090702-def0-5eac-8760-9a3b321889de" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392044 #edb/ref 1080 "-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392044 #edb/ref 1082