 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{2}{5} & -\\frac{2}{5} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are two pivot columns (the $1$st and the $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we obtain ${x}_{2}={x}_{3}.$ Substituting this in the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{5}(2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(2{x}_{3}+3{x}_{3}) \\\\  & ={x}_{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting, for instance, ${x}_{3}=1,$ we get the eigenvector\n$v=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186399188 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399189 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399188 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399190 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399188 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399191 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399188 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399192 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399188 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399193 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399188 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399188 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399188 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186399189 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399188 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "adc9838b-0769-5bf4-b3d7-c8c2300681dc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399189 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186399189 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399189 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "88495c5e-727c-5bdc-8c66-f5f7a1da7068" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399190 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 20\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186399190 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399190 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "973ba97a-cf4d-57f4-b6a7-6d7f845916bc